{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/3D Camera Solve from Feature Tracks.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/3D Camera Solve from Feature Tracks.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"3 d camera solve from feature tracks 3 d camera solve from feature tracks","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/3D Camera Solve from Feature Tracks.md","fileName":"3D Camera Solve from Feature Tracks.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"3D Camera Solve from Feature Tracks","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-15 18:17\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[CG Integration and Render Passes]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["CG Integration and Render Passes","Parallax as a 3D Matchmove Cue","digitalvisualeffectsandcompositing.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/3D Camera Solve from Feature Tracks.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/3D Camera Solve from Feature Tracks.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"3 d camera solve from feature tracks 3 d camera solve from feature tracks","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/3D Camera Solve from Feature Tracks.md","fileName":"3D Camera Solve from Feature Tracks.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"3D Camera Solve from Feature Tracks","heading":"3D Camera Solve from Feature Tracks","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"A 3D matchmove uses many image-feature tracks to infer the motion and orientation of the camera through a scene. Features with poor confidence or belonging to moving subjects should be filtered or masked before solving. The resulting camera path and point cloud require a useful scene origin and orientation, then a test object should be rendered to see whether it remains locked to the filmed environment. One- or two-point image transforms cannot supply the same depth-dependent motion. See [[Parallax as a 3D Matchmove Cue]].","tags":["baby"],"links":["